      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Discarding Mantle of the Ancients is reasonable since it's expensive (5 mana) and its recursion ability requires Auras/Equipment in the graveyard to get value. However, Mantle of the Ancients has synergy with Galea (the commander, who casts Auras/Equipment from library top) and could be a powerful late-game finisher in this Aura/Equipment-focused deck. Verdant Embrace (also 5 mana) is arguably less synergistic with the deck's core strategy - it's just a stat boost and token generator with no particular Equipment/Aura synergy beyond being an Aura itself. That said, Mantle is more situational (needs graveyard targets) while Verdant Embrace is independently strong. The choice is close enough to be debatable.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Mantle of the Ancients",
      "better_line": "Discarding Verdant Embrace could be slightly better since Mantle of the Ancients has stronger synergy with the Galea Equipment/Aura strategy and can recursively attach multiple pieces from the graveyard later in the game. However, this is genuinely close.",
