    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gryff's Boon has a built-in recursion ability ({3}{W}: Return from graveyard to battlefield attached to a creature), making it actively better in the graveyard than in hand for a deck that cares about auras/equipment. Additionally, Mantle of the Ancients is already in the graveyard, which returns Auras and Equipment from the graveyard - so having Gryff's Boon in the graveyard is fine. However, the real consideration is that Gryff's Boon's recursion ability means discarding it loses very little value. The issue is more about what else could have been discarded. Verdant Embrace at {3}{G}{G} is very expensive and the deck appears to be Bant (GWU) with limited mana development (no lands in play yet for Llama4 Coach based on the board state showing only the other players' boards). Verdant Embrace is the hardest card to cast and least synergistic with the equipment/aura Voltron strategy compared to other options. That said, Gryff's Boon being recursive from the graveyard makes it a reasonable discard choice - but Verdant Embrace would have been slightly better to discard as it's the most expensive and least aligned with the deck's core strategy.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Gryff's Boon",
