    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Qwen3 Sarge has 3 artifacts (Ancient Den, Darksteel Citadel, Arcane Signet) and could play Exotic Orchard instead of Mountain. Exotic Orchard is a land that taps for any color opponents' lands produce (Plains, Island, Forest are all on board), giving access to W, U, G in addition to whatever else. More importantly, Exotic Orchard would be a strictly better land drop here since it produces more colors. However, the real consideration is that playing Exotic Orchard preserves the Mountain in hand for a future turn where it could be equally played. The key issue is that with 4 lands (3 current + 1 new), Arcane Signet gives access to R/W colors. Next turn with 5 mana, Pia Nalaar (2R) could be cast either way. But Exotic Orchard produces more flexible mana - it can tap for W, U, G, or potentially R if opponents play Mountains later. Mountain only taps for R. Since Arcane Signet already provides R, Exotic Orchard would have been the better land drop for mana flexibility, especially since the hand contains both red cards (Pia Nalaar, Hellkite Tyrant) and white cards (Bronze Guardian, Digsite Engineer) and Exotic Orchard can produce white from opponents' Plains.",
